## Interface: 16001
## AllowLoadGameType: camelot
## ExcludeLoadGameType: standard, classic
## Title: Tx Example
## Notes: One sentence that says what this addon does.
## Author: Tx Studio
## Version: @project-version@
## Category: Tx Studio
## SavedVariables: TxExampleDB
## OptionalDeps: LibTx-1.0
## X-License: MIT
## X-Website: https://github.com/YOUR-ORG/Tx_Example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Game flavors. One TOC for every client; bump the numbers on patch day (PATCH_DAY.md).
#   16001  = WoW: Forever 1.60.1 (every beta build so far; re-check on the launch client)
#
# Forever only (the default): the two LoadGameType lines at the top keep the addon off
# retail and Classic, even where they share one AddOns folder with Forever. "camelot" is
# the client's name for Forever; every tested client knows "standard" (retail) and
# "classic" (the Classic flavors). Use only these words: a client ignores game types it
# does not know, so an Allow line alone does not keep the addon off retail or Classic,
# and no Blizzard TOC uses "forever". Details: README.md, "Game flavors and the TOC".
#
# Also retail and/or Classic Era? Delete the two LoadGameType lines and append the numbers:
#   ## Interface: 16001, 120105, 11509
#   120105 = retail 12.1.5      11509 = Classic Era 1.15.9
# then add the flavor to SUPPORTED_FLAVORS in Core.lua. Check a client's number in game
# with: /dump (select(4, GetBuildInfo()))
#
# Never add a second TOC with "## Interface: 00000" (an "unsupported client" stub): the
# packager reads it as retail and tags the CurseForge and Wago uploads for retail too.
# Split into Tx_Example_Camelot.toc (never _Forever.toc: the packager ignores that suffix)
# and Tx_Example_Mainline.toc only when the clients need different file lists.
#
# Upload IDs read by the BigWigs packager. 0 = do not upload. Keep these lines even while
# they are 0: a missing line lets the packager borrow the ID of another folder in the zip.
# The CurseForge ID can go in as soon as the project exists: CI uploads to CurseForge only
# once the repository variable CURSEFORGE_UPLOADS is "on" (RELEASING.md).
#   X-Curse-Project-ID = number in the "About Project" box on CurseForge
#   X-Wago-ID          = project ID from the Wago Addons developer dashboard
#   X-WoWI-ID          = WoWInterface addon number (WoWInterface does not list Forever)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## X-Curse-Project-ID: 0
## X-Wago-ID: 0
## X-WoWI-ID: 0

# Shared team library, fetched into Libs\ by the packager (.pkgmeta externals).
#@no-lib-strip@
Libs\LibTx-1.0\LibStub\LibStub.lua
Libs\LibTx-1.0\LibTx-1.0.lua
#@end-no-lib-strip@

Locales\enUS.lua
Core.lua
